# Set a Minimum, Preferred, and Maximum

```css
h1 {
  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
}
```
- Minimum: 1.5rem (never smaller)
- Preferred: 5vw (5% of viewport width, grows with screen)
- Maximum: 3rem (never larger)

The browser picks the preferred value, clamped between min and max. This creates fluid scaling without breakpoints.
